  "brief": 242,
  "observations": "The seven core plates and previously delivered denatured enzyme are available. The full-size thermometer has no printed scale or numerals. Its red column is baked into the artwork, so place the live temperature readout separately. The skin plates keep their different vessel and hair features on cream.\n\nThe 1,254-square denatured enzyme is the commissioned FA1 v20 asset. It has visibly changed pocket shape but contains no free gold substrate. The 2,000-square bound image includes the substrate, and the two full silhouettes overlap by about 76%. The existing v20 registration evidence supports a separate painted substrate and the induced-fit pairing. The v33 named fallback remains the build handoff for the combined bound-to-denatured view. The temperature steps are illustrative inputs and should drive the marker and bars from the same timeline.",
